## 1. Task List

These tasks execute the approved design; the PRD remains the acceptance source. Evidence files named below are planned outputs beneath this run's artefact directory, not completed checks. The implementing agent owns execution and cooperative reviews; Arndt Gold retains human approval and actual UAT authority. No delegation is required.

| task_id | Task | Owner | Dependencies |
|---|---|---|---|
| T-001 | After valid TP approval, complete renewed routed Brownfield Analysis; capture approved-source hashes, commit/index/dirty paths, retained implementation and resource-limit reproduction; inspect existing Core filesystem/evaluation/backlog, worker/session, DTO/HTTP/UI and assembly owners, dependency reads and propagation before edits; document canonical backlog writers, their lock/revision/journal boundary and which gate operations do not synchronize backlog | Implementing agent | TP approval and canonical preparation route |
| T-002 | Requalify pinned private SDK/lock and self-contained build, resource/CSP/theme constraints; retain existing build ownership and prohibit dependency contamination or version substitution | UI implementing agent | T-001 |
| T-003 | Implement bounded dependency recording, containment and descriptor/ancestor stability, freeze/revalidation/replay under existing Core read seam; project only Master Backlog for overview, evaluate direct named Run with genuine Core dependencies, then registered document/context scopes; preserve broad capture API and fixed limits | Core/UI implementing agent | T-001 |
| T-004 | Update strict optional snapshot run_id and discriminated backlog/run/document/context DTOs with scoped transitions in existing worker/session/wire owner; validate incoming selectors before discard, drop old capture before replacement, issue matching parents/new IDs, reject late or failed replacement; requalify four independent live/retiring slots and existing completion schema | MCP/Core implementing agent | T-002, T-003 |
| T-005 | Rebuild schema, shared browser/MCP UI and self-contained resource together via existing assembly/local preparation owners; prepare minimal shared direct-Run/backlog reading route, typed errors and named owned runtime; retain default/public inventory and exact provenance, prepare fresh discovery | Assembly/MCP/UI implementing agent | T-004 |
| T-006 | Qualify minimal revised path early in actual Codex: current schema/resource/runtime tuple, backlog-only and direct named opening under unchanged 64 MiB bound in the evidence-heavy target, requested/displayed identity, two independent readable views and usable larger surface; separately requalify advertised bridge capabilities without automatic test messages | Implementing agent; Arndt Gold for deliberate interactive action | T-005; authorized supported host activation |
| T-007 | Requalify exact run-owned graph projection in new context replacement scope; retain matching parent Run/current document, fresh opaque nodes, explicit empty/unresolved/limit states and no recursive evidence reads | Core implementing agent | T-006 feasibility checkpoint passed |
| T-008 | Requalify registered-source packet provenance/size/freshness and exclusive publication ownership against replacement captures; retain reserve-before-prepare, owned invalidation/acknowledged completion, bounded receipt, never-published failure release and uncertain-owner quarantine while other views read | Core implementing agent | T-007 |
| T-009 | Finish shared React/HTTP/MCP scoped DTO validation and navigation/reducer: matching parent bundles, new opaque resource rebinding and stable registered return focus; backlog stored labels/counts and file-observation freshness distinct from Run currentness, including Run-only approval with unchanged backlog; failure without zero Runs/empty selector, deliberate current-scope retry; preserve Pages header/fonts/colors/spacing, summary/detail, immutable session ports and responsive accessibility | UI implementing agent | T-006 passed, T-007 |
| T-010 | Requalify serialized session-bound context publication/question/invalidation through new read transitions; acknowledge context before deliberate question and owned host invalidation before matched completion; preserve nonowner no-update, completion-only retry, uncertainty and no automatic question resend | UI implementing agent | T-008, T-009 |
| T-011 | Execute renewed read-set, Core parity, scope/selector/replay race, limits, session/publication, UI/browser and default-runtime compatibility scenarios, including canonical backlog transaction regressions and unsynchronized-approval reading; inspect actual diff and renewed task fulfilment through required reviews, repair scoped findings and record reproducible failures/results | Implementing agent; routed review owners | T-010 |
| T-012 | Record complete current native journey and multi-view qualification, app-only no-write window, owned rollback/reconnect, implemented architecture/setup with precise backlog write/synchronization/observation limits and verified graph reconciliation; distinguish historical results and gaps for canonical QA/UAT/OR | Implementing agent; Arndt Gold for UAT | T-011 |

T-002 through T-005 requalify retained code and implement only the renewed minimal scoped-read contract, shared initial routing/error DTOs and trusted runtime/resource path needed for T-006. Existing graph/publication code remains retained and must not be asserted absent or automatically accepted. Extensive new graph/handoff adaptation follows T-006. A fresh feasibility checkpoint tests reading/current tuple first; already accepted synthetic questions are not repeated. If a new context/message probe is necessary, record why and obtain a distinct deliberate action at send time; no new question authorization is created by this plan. A missing required host capability leaves its acceptance evidence open and stops dependent feature expansion; browser or protocol success is never substitution.

