## 3. Test Plan

### Execution and evidence ordering

1. After TP approval, complete renewed T-001 through canonical Brownfield Analysis, distinguishing archived approvals and retained implementation/results from current evidence. Capture approved hashes and dirty/index/runtime baseline, inspect actual Core dependency closure and containment seam, preserve unrelated human changes and identify minimal propagation before edits.
2. T-002 through T-005 add scoped recording/freeze/replay under the existing read owner, backlog parser projection, direct selected-Run evaluation and discriminated wire/HTTP/UI transitions together. Prove real dependency read sets, unchanged Core evaluation and selector/candidate-lifetime boundaries before local preparation. Retain fixed worker/session/capture budgets; do not raise the global limit, delete evidence or create a second evaluator. Prepare matched schema/resource and minimal route/error rendering, rebuild both transports and owned runtime with exact digest read-back. No plugin-cache/global configuration write is implied.
3. T-006 is the fresh minimal native checkpoint: observe new descriptor/resource/runtime identity, empty backlog and direct established Run opening in the evidence-heavy target, requested/displayed identity, available surface/width and two independently readable views. Prior feasibility remains dated; do not repeat accepted synthetic messages. Any newly necessary probe remains separately deliberate and labelled; current bridge/source/model proof is kept distinct. Record inability to expose both native views as a gap rather than ask for completed approvals again.
4. Requalify retained graph/packet/ownership features in T-007/T-008; finish shared transition navigation, stable source focus, stored backlog/error semantics and serialized owned handoff in T-009/T-010. Then T-011 executes mapped integration/compatibility tests and required actual-diff/task reviews. Scenario counts are traceability coverage, not a promised number of executable tests or permission to weaken assertions.
5. T-012 collects final current native source/context/question and multi-view evidence, no-write window, owned rollback/reconnect, implemented architecture/setup with precise backlog write/synchronization/observation limits and verified graph reconciliation. Deliberate source questions already accepted historically are not automatically replayed; missing new action/host access remains explicit. QA pass/revise/block, human QA/UAT approvals and OR/closeout remain separate.

### Automated checks and planned test ownership

Use supported Node 22.22.3 already available, preserving project engine support. Changed and additional behavioral coverage belongs beside existing owners, including packages/core/test/cockpit-session-test.js for registry/publication ownership and packages/control-ui/test/handoff.test.tsx for immutable ports and two-sided release: `packages/core/test/cockpit-context-test.js` for graph/packet/limits; `packages/cli/scripts/cockpit-mcp-test.js` for strict local mode/session/composition/provenance; existing `packages/mcp-server` tests for SDK registration/resource/tool wire behavior; existing private UI test lanes for shared transport, rendering, bridge controller and build. These are planned files/coverage, not commands already executed.

Run the resulting Core/CLI tests with Node; run `npm --prefix packages/mcp-server test`, `npm --prefix packages/control-ui run typecheck`, `npm --prefix packages/control-ui run build`, `npm --prefix packages/control-ui test` and `npm --prefix packages/control-ui run test:browser`. Reuse the existing npm --prefix packages/control-ui run build:mcp script under the Vite owner; record exact command/output and assembled resource digest. Protocol tests must cover supported negotiated protocol eras where SDK/host actually support them; do not claim unsupported-era compatibility from schema inspection.

Run affected existing regressions: `packages/core/test/control-state-test.js`, `packages/cli/scripts/control-command-test.js`, `packages/cli/scripts/control-inspect-test.js`, `packages/core/test/interaction-presentation-test.js`, `packages/cli/scripts/plugin-mcp-runtime-test.js`, `packages/cli/scripts/mcp-lifecycle-test.js`, `packages/cli/scripts/runtime-integrity-layout-test.js`, `packages/cli/scripts/runtime-integrity-negative-test.js`, `packages/cli/scripts/local-preparation-test.js`, `packages/cli/scripts/package-contents-test.js` and `packages/cli/scripts/payload-budget-test.js`. Also run assembler/local-development tests that own changed profile/preparation branches. Existing verification owners continue supplying required checks; no new parallel verification framework. Public/default inventory comparison is meaningful because UI dependencies must stay private. If assembly needs generated prerequisites, use the existing synchronization/preparation owner before testing; record exact output profile and prerequisite ordering.

Boundary tests use disposable controlled files/registered sources. Include one real filesystem control tree above 64 MiB, with unrelated historical evidence, and production worker/stdio operations proving small scopes open; do not mutate or remove real historical evidence. A retained live-target native check confirms the same fix on the actual resource-heavy target. Record byte and dependency/evaluator traces, not only a success assertion. Fake clocks cover expiry without hours of waiting. Inject controlled source mutation/read/bridge responses for race reproduction, retaining at least one real stdio integration and real captured filesystem lane. Capture response/packet UTF-8 sizes using the same serialized form sent to the host. Source/schema/default-profile failure tests must prove the actual production boundary, not a test-only guard.

### Master Backlog: deterministic writing versus observation authority

The existing canonical writer remains the owner of backlog mutation. Its run-step path serializes the Run lock then the shared Backlog lock, compares expected revisions/current bytes, writes each file by atomic replacement and uses the Run commit point plus transaction journal/recovery for the multi-file result. This is not an indivisible filesystem-wide write and not an exclusive OS permission preventing direct editor writes. Requalify existing regression coverage; the cockpit must not add a writer or a second synchronization policy.

The current approveRunGate path writes the sealed Run and does not atomically refresh the Master Backlog. prepareBacklog preserves an existing status unless an operation explicitly supplies a replacement, and a missing backlog can be reported without an update. Thus safe deterministic write mechanics do not guarantee every pointer is complete, unique, or synchronized after every gate operation. T-001 records these precise boundaries; unsupported/missing/duplicate pointer behavior remains visible through the approved parser/reading scope.

Make the three claims distinguishable in data/feedback and verification: (1) stored backlog status/next step from identified captured backlog bytes; (2) currentness of that file observation against its dependency set; (3) the selected Run's currently observed Core evaluation/revision and prerequisites. A fresh backlog file may contain an older stored next step after a Run-only approval. Do not label that observation an up-to-date Run, a confirmed gate, authorization or synchronized control inventory. Native/browser wording and styles must preserve this distinction without forcing raw-source interpretation. No extra Run scan/evaluation merely to decorate backlog rows.

SCN-079 is the concrete regression: deliberately approve only a disposable fixture Run through its existing canonical presentation/approval path, observe unchanged backlog bytes and changed Run revision, then prove stored pointer versus checked selected-Run feedback. Fixture approval never uses this live Run or a replayed human reply. SCN-080 checks semantic deterministic projection; SCN-081 the unchanged canonical transaction owner; SCN-082 capture/pending boundaries; SCN-083 no automatic persistence repair. Every result records relevant hashes, action, actual outcome and any gap. Canonical setup/mutations happen outside app-only no-write windows. The transaction tests observed during earlier diagnosis are baseline evidence, not a substitute for renewed implementation verification.

This plan implements the approved read-side contract. Synchronizing every gate approval into the backlog would modify the canonical write/control contract; it requires the earliest affected source revision and renewed design rather than being silently added to these tasks. T-001/T-011 report any writer defect to that existing owner and scope route. They must not increase read scope, mutate backlog from the cockpit, or treat the known synchronization boundary as an exception to Core safety checks.

### Manual and actual-host checks

Check card, expanded detail and passive source at 320/560/800/1280px in the browser, measuring container width, scrollWidth, columns and header height rather than assuming the host viewport. In the native host record the actual available container/display mode separately; do not infer native width from browser screenshots. Exercise the 640px container breakpoint, search without selection changes, counted expandable source notices, unchanged Pages branding and readable wrapping. Use keyboard and pointer journeys at supported narrow/wide sizes and the actual native panel/display mode: compact entry, explicit run selection, source identity, passive artefact, maintained graph node, inclusion/exclusion, preparation, context acceptance and deliberate question. Custom follow-up uses Codex's existing composer. Verify visible context/source identity without claiming acknowledgement proves a correct answer. Preserve source/protocol, browser, actual-host and human-UAT results separately; fixture/browser successes cannot satisfy a missing actual-host criterion.

The no-write window hashes canonical control bytes immediately before and after app-only operations, including context and question. No agent control bookkeeping or graph curation occurs inside that window. Later evidence writes occur outside it and cannot be used to conceal an app mutation. A live later delivery request, if exercised, uses the installed independent connection and fresh canonical binding; never send an approval string or implementation request as the app's test question.

Evidence records scenario ID, exact fixture or project source identity, command/action, observed expected/actual outcome, time, runtime/UI digest, and any failure/uncertainty. Reports use bounded logs without session secrets. Test skips, inaccessible capabilities and stale earlier results remain gaps. Cooperative self-review is labelled and never described as independent review.

### Scoped-read and per-view verification boundaries

The existing Core read/capture filesystem seam owns bounded dependency recording and frozen replay. Enumerations and observed missing paths are genuine inputs; do not fabricate missing data because a path was not loaded. Core's selected-Run resolver may enumerate/read all Run metadata for a legitimate policy check; this is distinct from fully evaluating every Run or reading unrelated images. Trace exact dependency closure on genuine Core calls, and compare frozen selected-Run output/diagnostics with unchanged evaluation on the same stable fixtures. Seal validation may read registered bytes before presentation. Never weaken that validation to claim no document reads. Broad capture consumers retain existing behavior.

Overview captures only Master Backlog plus containment anchors and labels stored pointers. Missing/unsupported/duplicate/malformed entries cannot become a valid/complete Run inventory. Direct named capture has no overview prerequisite or membership requirement. Initial failure remains identified; only positively confirmed removal of an already valid inspected Run returns to backlog. UI and both adapters share discriminated scope validation; refresh rebuilds the current requested scope deliberately. New document/context parents and opaque registrations agree with a new immutable snapshot; return focus uses stable registered identity, not an old opaque ID.

Check incoming selectors before discarding a valid view. Then discard own old capture and invalidate packet before constructing candidate, keeping one retained capture per view and fixed aggregate source budget. Failed/cancelled/late candidate does not resurrect prior selectors. Missing/denied/deadline/limit feedback labels old content previous; unread overview does not show zero counts/search/empty selector. Foreign selectors leave legitimate current scope usable. Read-scope transition must preserve existing publication ownership/acknowledgement sequencing and other views.

T-003/T-004 requalify four live/retiring slots, one lazy worker per slot, one active/one queued job, 64 MiB dependency bytes per MCP view/256 MiB aggregate, 256 MiB worker old-generation, individual file/preview/response/count/depth/deadline bounds and independent timers. A retired worker counts until actual teardown; shutdown/partial allocation/cancel cannot revive sessions or expand resources. No total-RSS promise. Browser limits are unchanged. T-008/T-010 requalify exclusive publication reserve/prepare/validate/begin/ack/complete/uncertainty under actual production controllers. Old callbacks remain bound to their own session; no nonowner update, timed takeover or automatic accepted question repetition.

Reuse existing deterministic fixture, fake-clock, deferred-response, controlled filesystem and real worker/stdio lanes. Test recording, freeze, replay and final revalidation mutations, observed absence/enumeration, symlink/ancestor/descriptor swaps and unexpected replay dependencies with production seams. Unobserved historical mutation must not invalidate the scope; relevant dependency change must. Compare control bytes across app-only windows, separating later evidence writes. Positive cases and fail-closed limits remain required together.

The final native two-view window includes equal/distinct-Run reads, own scope/close behavior, competing handoff refusal, acknowledged release and a subsequent separately deliberate source transfer/question. Concurrent reachable views must share the exact loaded connection; sequential screenshots and old/expired panels do not prove independence. Lost owner requires qualified fresh connection/host-context currentness, not an empty server record or historical-chat erasure claim. After verified implementation update docs/architecture/06-agdf-cockpit.md and affected existing references with scoped read flow, immutable replacement/provenance, limits and diagnosis. Do not overwrite unrelated dirty diagram changes. Graph curation accepts verified facts through existing closeout ownership only.

## 4. Brownfield Scope

Inspect and reuse `packages/core/lib/control-read/`, `control-inspect/cockpit.js`, run parser/evaluator and Core composition; `packages/control-ui/server/pool.mjs`, `read-worker.mjs`, HTTP/session wrappers, `src/App.tsx`, `state.ts`, `api.ts`, `types.ts`, existing views and Vite owner; `packages/mcp-server/bin/`, `src/` and its tests; `packages/cli/lib/mcp-dispatch-runtime.js`, local development preparation and `mcp-lifecycle/package.js`; `scripts/assemble-npm.mjs` and owned profile/package checks. The approved SD owns module boundaries and versions. Reuse control-evaluation/shared.js backlog/table parsing, the control-read FS seam and capture owner, unchanged run-state resolver/evaluateGateCheck, and shared cockpit DTO/reducer owners; no new status database, filesystem policy engine or parallel authority. Wrapper compatibility is verified rather than retaining a second worker implementation.

Only current-run control artefacts and necessary implementation/derived paths belong to this scope. Existing dirty MASTER_BACKLOG/current-run records are process state, not permission to alter unrelated runs. `.agdf/control/CONTEXT_GRAPH.md` remains maintained knowledge; curate verified implementation facts into existing appropriate nodes through closeout, preserving the open impact until evidence exists. Do not create graph relationships merely from planning. Installed AGDF/default runtime, protected host settings, unrelated projects and the existing browser process are not general repair targets.

## 5. Out Of Scope

Graph editor/database, inferred relevance, recursive context crawling, automatic completeness/Soll-Ist evaluation, generic filesystem/shell/network tools, gate/approval writers, automatic contextual questions, a second chat composer, persistent app selection/packet storage, remote/multiuser/public deployment, broad plugin/cache repair, new host adapters, public SDK/runtime migration, commit/push/PR/release/publication and transfer of prior browser-run approvals. No architecture/version fallback without the applicable source revision route. This change adds no server per card, persistent session registry, inter-iframe bus or host adapter.

## 6. Risks And Blockers

| Risk or trigger | Required response and evidence owner |
|---|---|
| Exact SDK packages unavailable, incompatible or contaminate the owned server graph | Stop dependency/build lane; record registry/build evidence and route SD revision before substitution; UI/MCP owner |
| Actual host cannot load named app, provide usable larger view or accept required context/message methods | T-006 blocks extensive dependent feature work; preserve precise feasibility gap and fallback, route design/evidence owner; never declare embedded completion from mocks |
| Protected configuration/registration workflow unavailable | Preserve ready reviewable entry and use supported authorized workflow only; external permission/state gap stays explicit, not a silently edited global config |
| Source/selector/provenance mismatch, unexpected replay dependency, containment/mutation/limit or invalidation uncertainty | Reject/block affected handoff with exact reason; Core/UI owner fixes and reruns affected scenarios |
| New private cockpit DTO/parent mismatch, browser/default MCP or owned assembly regression | Block QA, repair within approved scope and rerun directly affected compatibility checks; scope growth routes back to earliest affected gate |
| Stale descriptor/bootstrap, foreign or unavailable initial Run | Reject invalid selectors, retain requested identity and fresh-session generation checks; prepare matched schema/UI and record a fresh actual host discovery before claiming direct opening; MCP/UI owner |
| Publication ownership cannot be safely completed or host context outcome is uncertain | Keep exclusive handoff blocked while reads remain usable; require matched acknowledged completion or qualified fresh connection, never timed takeover; Core/UI and host evidence owners |
| Native host cannot expose two concurrent views on one connection | Keep SCN-059/060 and affected acceptance evidence open; record observed host limitation without treating sequential panels or browser fixtures as proof; host evidence owner |
| Missing live-host/no-write/rollback/graph knowledge evidence | Keep criterion/closeout open; QA/OR owners decide readiness, no presumed acceptance |
| Historical model context persists after lost host/process or later source edit | Record bounded observation and limitation; disable uncertain new handoff and require fresh validation for later use, without claiming historical messages can be erased |
| Fresh backlog bytes still contain an older pointer after Run-only approval | Label stored pointer and file observation separately from selected Core evaluation; SCN-079 is mandatory. An all-gate writer synchronization requires applicable source revision, never implicit scope growth; Core/UI owners |
| A genuine selected-Run Core dependency still exceeds fixed limits | Return the exact resource_limit/identity; inspect scope with existing owner, never increase capacities, omit required checks or delete evidence silently; material change requires earliest affected source revision |
| Concurrent human file/index changes overlap the implementation lane | Preserve them, re-evaluate current baseline and reconcile only scoped paths; no staging/reset or unrelated diagram overwrite |

No debt waiver, authority shortcut or second source of truth is accepted. A material implementation discovery that changes approved scope/design goes through canonical revision rather than editing approved PRD/SD bytes.

## 7. Next Step

Review and approve only with `Approval: TP`. Valid approval permits the routed Brownfield Analysis and then scoped implementation once its prerequisites are satisfied. It does not approve QA/UAT/OR, protected host writes outside permission, version substitution or VCS/release actions.

